[7025]={["aftermath"]="Greatfather Winter thanked the helper and offered a small holiday gift.",["atomIDs"]={"7025:description:1-70","7025:description:75-212","7025:description:215-306","7025:description:309-377","7025:objective:1-84"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7025:completion:1-60","7025:completion:63-96","7025:completion:101-128","7025:completion:130-154"},["opening"]="Greatfather Winter wanted a break from a full day of visitors. Five gingerbread cookies and cold milk were the treat he requested in Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to fetch the cookies and milk.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Greatfather Winter the requested treats.",["sourceHash"]="e4cf481cb1f99d4b61106cc6ac9a04ba01c3841074a55b9787504155dc1cc35b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7026]={["aftermath"]="The commander intended to announce when enough hides had been gathered.",["atomIDs"]={"7026:description:1-57","7026:description:130-262","7026:description:264-293","7026:description:298-400","7026:description:402-472","7026:description:59-125","7026:objective:1-4"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7026:completion:1-19","7026:completion:21-81","7026:completion:86-94"},["objectiveSummary"]="Bring frostwolf hides to the Stormpike Ram Rider Commander.",["opening"]="The Stormpikes needed harness leather without slaughtering their own prospective mounts. Their commander chose frostwolf hides instead, turning the enemy's cavalry animals into supplies for the brigade's rams.",["pending"]="{actor} would gather frostwolf hides for Stormpike riding harnesses.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought hides to the Stormpike ram rider commander.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="3ceb4e1ff969090a27235a3de6daa4d0b3935ed060b96b2f63980f0d02a85fa9",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7027]={["aftermath"]="The stable master encouraged further captures toward the restoration of the cavalry.",["atomIDs"]={"7027:description:1-29","7027:description:31-36","7027:description:38-104","7027:description:109-134","7027:description:136-196","7027:description:198-283","7027:description:285-365","7027:description:370-435","7027:description:437-479","7027:objective:1-40","7027:objective:42-129","7027:objective:131-200","7027:objective:202-261"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7027:completion:1-43","7027:completion:45-66"},["opening"]="The Stormpike stables stood empty, leaving their cavalry unable to take the field. A training collar could snare an Alterac ram, but the animal still had to be led safely back before it could join the stable.",["pending"]="{actor} would collar an Alterac ram and bring it to the stable master.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned with a captured ram for the Stormpike stables.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="96cd90622fb9b5eae6ef772b3ace10bb9a5a3e8c2f74cc347562802d777e8746",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7028]={["aftermath"]="Willow's muttering revealed contempt for how readily a promised payment had secured the work.",["atomIDs"]={"7028:description:1-72","7028:description:74-114","7028:description:116-166","7028:description:168-224","7028:description:229-333","7028:description:335-405","7028:description:410-454","7028:description:456-466","7028:description:468-509","7028:objective:1-61"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7028:completion:11-31","7028:completion:36-51","7028:completion:56-78","7028:completion:83-122","7028:completion:124-137"},["opening"]="Willow sought ancient relics in Maraudon's crystal caverns. She wanted the carvings for study and hinted at powers she believed had rested too long.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to recover fifteen crystal carvings for Willow.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered fifteen Theradric Crystal Carvings.",["sourceHash"]="c977107365418c7549f4da3439399b7bf8dee68064adc178f726523b5a67a562",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7029]={["aftermath"]="Vark welcomed the remaining liquid for study and credited the work with healing part of the corruption, while leaving more to do.",["atomIDs"]={"7029:description:1-116","7029:description:121-139","7029:description:141-286","7029:description:291-377","7029:description:379-474","7029:description:476-503","7029:objective:1-69","7029:objective:74-172","7029:objective:177-276"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7029:completion:1-33","7029:completion:35-102","7029:completion:107-226","7029:completion:228-262"},["opening"]="Vark sought to heal vines damaged by Vyletongue's corruption. The vial's coating would purify water from the orange pool, though the treated plants could still lash out under the satyr's influence.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to use the vial and defeat the scions to heal eight plants.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Vark after treating eight vines and defeating their corrupted scions.",["sourceHash"]="fd0fc5679cb3b2da467b4c04a7171b80d30eb0853b3ff2ecec62c150df766e59",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7041]={["aftermath"]="Talendria retained the remaining liquid for research and recognized the partial healing of Maraudon's corruption.",["atomIDs"]={"7041:description:1-116","7041:description:121-139","7041:description:141-288","7041:description:293-379","7041:description:381-476","7041:description:478-505","7041:objective:1-69","7041:objective:74-172","7041:objective:177-265"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7041:completion:1-33","7041:completion:35-102","7041:completion:107-226","7041:completion:228-262"},["opening"]="Talendria offered a vial that could turn the orange pool's toxins into a healing agent. Treating the vines would purge corruption but could force out hostile scions.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to purify the water and heal eight vines by defeating their scions.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the treatment of eight plants to Talendria.",["sourceHash"]="f186f4da7e7e33fe04b32fc5b97081dd621cd344e93f4b6210b5cdc6028e6ea7",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7042]={["aftermath"]="The snowman identified himself as Sacks of Smokywood's Ironforge branch, transformed after an attack during the search.",["atomIDs"]={"7042:description:1-9","7042:description:11-155","7042:description:160-339","7042:description:342-452","7042:description:457-498","7042:objective:1-111"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7042:completion:1-24","7042:completion:26-51","7042:completion:56-176","7042:completion:178-303","7042:completion:308-326"},["opening"]="Wulmort had lost a shipment of holiday treats and the agent sent to find it. Their last trace led into the snowy Alterac Mountains.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to locate the missing Smokywood investigator.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} found the investigator in Alterac.",["sourceConflicts"]={"Finisher metadata names the Abominable Greench, but objective and completion concern the investigator Sacks as a snowman. Prose follows the text without resolving the metadata."},["sourceHash"]="79c4bb3ff70b7dc3b43430bb109493ab46082d1eef716273325dcf572566f1b0",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7043]={["aftermath"]="Wulmort promised a team to help Sacks, hoping to unfreeze him in time for the feast.",["atomIDs"]={"7043:description:1-103","7043:description:106-127","7043:description:130-186","7043:description:191-240","7043:description:243-337","7043:description:340-462","7043:objective:1-73","7043:objective:76-208"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7043:completion:1-13","7043:completion:16-69","7043:completion:74-86","7043:completion:88-163","7043:completion:166-273","7043:completion:276-335"},["opening"]="Sacks blamed the Greench for stealing the treats and turning him to snow. He asked for the shipment's return to Ironforge and help to undo his transformation.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover the stolen treats for Wulmort.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the shipment to Wulmort in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="083974a14c89467418df4429c2221e54855c0f949e674e102adf318665651e6c",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7044]={["aftermath"]="Celebras saw new hope that Maraudon might one day be free of the corruption.",["atomIDs"]={"7044:description:1-116","7044:description:118-161","7044:description:166-277","7044:description:279-343","7044:description:345-367","7044:description:369-416","7044:description:421-438","7044:description:440-482","7044:description:484-491","7044:objective:1-94","7044:objective:99-132"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7044:completion:1-125"},["opening"]="Cavindra asked for the two pieces of her brother's scepter, held by Vyletongue and Noxxion. Celebras himself wandered under corruption, so recovering them also required finding a way to reach him.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to recover the rod and diamond and speak with Celebras.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought together the Celebrian Rod and Diamond and reached Celebras.",["sourceHash"]="b5cb68aaf075149b9b0eb8557877f97bf55a3c8da5db7aa28e44b6559d1ff7d4",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7045]={["aftermath"]="Greatfather Winter presented the promised gift and wished the helper well for future feasts.",["atomIDs"]={"7045:description:1-74","7045:description:77-126","7045:description:128-183","7045:description:188-313","7045:description:316-396","7045:description:398-422","7045:objective:1-43"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7045:completion:1-24","7045:completion:29-140","7045:completion:142-228"},["opening"]="Wulmort arranged a special gift in thanks for the recovered treats. Greatfather Winter would present Smokywood's acknowledgment in Ironforge.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to meet Greatfather Winter.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Greatfather Winter in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="4e7886d472e0c4f42c4bc3131e172983fd55556da4d141d4d39cecc58039b961",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7046]={["aftermath"]="Celebras entrusted its power for good use and sent the journey onward toward his uncle's remains, warning of dangers still ahead.",["atomIDs"]={"7046:description:1-44","7046:description:46-118","7046:description:120-174","7046:description:176-211","7046:description:216-312","7046:description:314-433","7046:description:438-498","7046:objective:1-70","7046:objective:75-117"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7046:completion:1-84","7046:completion:86-181","7046:completion:183-209","7046:completion:214-255"},["opening"]="Celebras's scepter had once let him travel swiftly through the caverns in search of peace for his uncle. Restoring its rod and diamond required help with his ritual.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to assist Celebras through the reunion ritual.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} helped Celebras complete the scepter's restoration.",["sourceHash"]="398fc671f216542e2f012c6c2740a1a1bc2a16e5295a494075c2ed70d5cefd32",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7061]={["aftermath"]="Cairne valued remembrance even amid the goblins' commercial revival, and praised the wish to understand the past beyond its material gifts.",["atomIDs"]={"7061:description:1-93","7061:description:96-267","7061:description:272-340","7061:description:343-451","7061:objective:1-88","7061:objective:91-175"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7061:completion:1-126","7061:completion:129-307","7061:completion:312-406","7061:completion:409-429"},["opening"]="Sagorne offered a collected account of the winter legends. After reading, the book was to reach Cairne, who would welcome an interest in the older lore.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to bring Sagorne's book to Cairne.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the winter lore book to Cairne in Thunder Bluff.",["sourceHash"]="a27768bcd61f6be8b531a13fe584c8aead6a0271377296cab7429c78db8359bd",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7062]={["aftermath"]="Karnik acknowledged Goli's bitterness while defending some celebration alongside remembrance of the feast's origins.",["atomIDs"]={"7062:description:1-26","7062:description:28-38","7062:description:43-123","7062:description:126-287","7062:description:292-412","7062:description:415-504","7062:objective:1-97"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7062:completion:1-34","7062:completion:36-104","7062:completion:106-241","7062:completion:246-308","7062:completion:310-378","7062:completion:380-483"},["opening"]="Goli objected to the holiday's focus on gifts and sweets. Karnik at the Explorers' League could explain the older legend of a land resting beneath winter's snow.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to ask Karnik about the feast's history.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} spoke with Historian Karnik in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="0facd42f2ac6f55269adf4af07e20e50ac6e80176be54c861c5f197b840e7046",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7063]={["aftermath"]="Magni saw value in keeping the lore alive despite the goblins' motives and praised the visitor's interest in the past.",["atomIDs"]={"7063:description:1-93","7063:description:96-256","7063:description:261-318","7063:description:321-424","7063:objective:1-88","7063:objective:91-177"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7063:completion:1-126","7063:completion:128-315","7063:completion:320-414","7063:completion:416-444"},["opening"]="Karnik offered a book gathering the feast's legends into one account. Its next destination was Magni, who would appreciate interest in the old stories.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to deliver Karnik's book to Magni.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought the book to King Magni in Ironforge.",["sourceHash"]="00162e8cc7131580a17aa4a5d29ba95860d5fee3276ef70323a9adb4927d6a4b",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7064]={["aftermath"]="Selendra welcomed news that the hardest task was done and planned to consult Marandis about Zaetar's remains.",["atomIDs"]={"7064:description:1-124","7064:description:126-195","7064:description:197-283","7064:description:285-366","7064:description:368-498","7064:objective:1-83"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7064:completion:1-32","7064:completion:34-43","7064:completion:48-183","7064:completion:188-287","7064:completion:289-358"},["opening"]="Selendra sought Theradras's defeat as the hardest step toward recovering Zaetar's remains. She traced the centaur's origins to the union that had ended in their father's death.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to defeat Theradras and return to Selendra.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported Theradras's defeat to Selendra.",["sourceHash"]="a284fdfd6b298abdd6f70a674d2df96cf043581063f19b2617dbb208ef014bbb",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7065]={["aftermath"]="Marandis accepted that the remains had not returned and deferred to Zaetar's will, hoping the centaur's bloodlust might lessen.",["atomIDs"]={"7065:description:1-65","7065:description:67-148","7065:description:150-211","7065:description:213-237","7065:description:239-286","7065:description:288-375","7065:description:377-507","7065:objective:1-83"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7065:completion:1-32","7065:completion:34-43","7065:completion:48-180","7065:completion:182-285","7065:completion:290-370","7065:completion:372-411"},["opening"]="Marandis wanted to recover Zaetar's remains from Maraudon after Theradras's defeat. He described the centaur as the children of that tragic union.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to defeat Theradras and report to Marandis.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned to Marandis after Theradras's defeat.",["sourceHash"]="210f2dd2aa3167ca84b6bcc5cd9c28a5b9187584164fcbbea3aae0f60e0b7daf",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7066]={["aftermath"]="Remulos found hope in his brother's peace and place within nature. He regarded the seed as a sign that Zaetar was reborn rather than lost.",["atomIDs"]={"7066:description:1-74","7066:description:79-161","7066:description:163-180","7066:description:182-221","7066:description:223-259","7066:description:264-331","7066:description:333-344","7066:description:346-411","7066:description:413-464","7066:description:466-494","7066:objective:1-60"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7066:completion:1-38","7066:completion:40-80","7066:completion:82-159","7066:completion:161-246","7066:completion:248-292","7066:completion:297-310","7066:completion:312-406","7066:completion:408-482","7066:completion:484-498"},["opening"]="Zaetar chose to remain where his body had nourished new life, even among the children who killed him. A first seed would carry that decision to his brother in Moonglade.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to bring Zaetar's seed and message to Remulos.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered the seed to Keeper Remulos.",["sourceHash"]="33f2416074b0802be423f2f7e9995812724047e9df78c7dfce89d6614432931b",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7067]={["aftermath"]="The pariah declared himself ready to begin uniting the tribes, hoping their next meeting would be on different terms.",["atomIDs"]={"7067:description:1-84","7067:description:86-152","7067:description:154-182","7067:description:187-326","7067:description:331-377","7067:description:379-433","7067:description:435-469","7067:objective:1-31","7067:objective:33-142"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7067:completion:1-15","7067:completion:17-27","7067:completion:29-81","7067:completion:83-92","7067:completion:97-131","7067:completion:133-193"},["opening"]="The exiled centaur needed an outsider to enter Maraudon's sacred halls. His written instructions led toward an amulet that could begin the destiny his own people had rejected.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to follow the instructions and recover the Amulet of Union.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the amulet to the Centaur Pariah.",["sourceHash"]="ad97a8ceee6cdc2c13815fd3ef420e2058e24c3ed23acbe0a952e714c547e5da",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7068]={["aftermath"]="Uthel'nay accepted the crystals for his magic and returned to his research.",["atomIDs"]={"7068:description:1-51","7068:description:53-79","7068:description:81-196","7068:description:201-285","7068:description:287-367","7068:description:372-433","7068:objective:1-89"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7068:completion:1-35","7068:completion:37-94","7068:completion:96-122"},["opening"]="Uthel'nay sought purple crystals from Maraudon's stone creatures. The magic protected within the centaur's holy place offered material for his studies.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to collect ten shadowshard fragments.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought ten fragments to Uthel'nay.",["sourceHash"]="1dec91053904e75ec1414a9c6b02e3df550d73c49e563f2b940b24129b500c34",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7070]={["aftermath"]="Tervosh welcomed the additional samples and offered trinkets already fashioned from earlier deliveries.",["atomIDs"]={"7070:description:1-73","7070:description:75-184","7070:description:186-283","7070:description:288-380","7070:description:382-444","7070:objective:1-129"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7070:completion:1-22","7070:completion:24-123","7070:completion:125-173","7070:completion:175-220"},["opening"]="Tervosh's research examined crystals and their arcane properties. With Proudmoore's leave, he sought specimens from the purple-stone elementals of Maraudon.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to recover ten fragments for Tervosh.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} delivered ten shadowshard fragments in Theramore.",["sourceHash"]="3a4f2099eb1b1cc79ef2b972f35b3e73033307938dcbac8f8cd7a74794e001c5",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7081]={["aftermath"]="Durgen urged renewed pressure on Horde-controlled graveyards.",["atomIDs"]={"7081:description:1-56","7081:description:59-130","7081:description:133-170","7081:description:175-215","7081:description:218-296","7081:description:299-341","7081:description:346-449","7081:objective:1-87"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7081:completion:1-10","7081:completion:12-65","7081:completion:67-136","7081:completion:141-151","7081:completion:153-227","7081:completion:229-248"},["opening"]="Durgen treated the valley's graveyards as vital ground. Pulling the banner at a Horde-held site would begin the assault; holding it until relief arrived was a further challenge, not something the initial attack alone guaranteed.",["pending"]="{actor} would assault an enemy graveyard and report to Durgen.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the graveyard assault to Sergeant Durgen Stormpike.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="ced3c46fa03648f3f89cf525456434089e72f253aa6bf1d12d4f4720f96da944",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7082]={["atomIDs"]={"7082:description:1-53","7082:description:56-130","7082:description:133-187","7082:description:192-239","7082:description:242-323","7082:description:328-380","7082:description:382-484","7082:objective:1-87"},["opening"]="Teeka's account of the valley followed its shifting borders, with graveyards at the fiercest points of dispute. Removing an Alliance banner would challenge their hold, while possession depended on keeping the ground afterward.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to assault an Alliance-held graveyard for Teeka.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the graveyard assault to Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="238f7a381b221f4902799ce66413c5f99b1692cad617e896d81d1e7d1388d7a3",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7101]={["aftermath"]="Teeka welcomed the report as an opportunity for the Horde's advance.",["atomIDs"]={"7101:description:1-82","7101:description:85-162","7101:description:167-212","7101:description:215-249","7101:description:252-323","7101:description:326-335","7101:description:340-495","7101:objective:1-90"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7101:completion:1-34","7101:completion:36-53","7101:completion:58-169"},["opening"]="Teeka wanted the Stormpike bunkers challenged from within. Replacing the inner banner began the capture, but destruction would follow only if the Horde held the position long enough and the Alliance failed to retake it.",["pending"]="{actor} would attack an enemy tower position and report to Teeka.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Teeka's assignment against the enemy tower position.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="ce25859ac70341171176602e3b4f121a95d97f6a026a1e406484132214c7f220",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7102]={["aftermath"]="Durgen's field report concerned the secured banner and the opportunity to move the line forward.",["atomIDs"]={"7102:description:1-88","7102:description:91-149","7102:description:154-207","7102:description:210-250","7102:description:253-327","7102:description:330-339","7102:description:344-491","7102:objective:1-114"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7102:completion:1-68","7102:completion:70-83","7102:completion:85-164"},["opening"]="For Durgen, towers and bunkers anchored the defense of Alterac. Securing an enemy banner would force its defenders out of position; razing the structure required a longer hold against any counterattack.",["pending"]="{actor} would seize an enemy tower's banner for the Stormpikes.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the captured banner to Durgen.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="b770928bb85c2e62c2a442304f7ddb0f2c95b1220aa65f771d92d3b5b03b1aab",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7121]={["aftermath"]="The quartermaster had further supply work to discuss.",["atomIDs"]={"7121:description:1-63","7121:description:66-167","7121:description:172-187","7121:description:190-231","7121:objective:1-39"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7121:completion:1-119","7121:completion:124-143","7121:completion:145-184"},["opening"]="Boombellow directed arriving recruits toward the Stormpike quartermaster. The army's needs extended below ground, where caches in Alterac's mines could support the men at the front.",["pending"]="{actor} would find the quartermaster west along the road.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported to the Stormpike quartermaster.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="57fe6f6d43e9c04ef4fd7a7cc2badaa78fedd6a1337f89af40ffc9ac0e4a2479",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7122]={["aftermath"]="Durgen expected a guarded mine to make mineral extraction and supply recovery easier.",["atomIDs"]={"7122:description:1-57","7122:description:60-158","7122:description:160-224","7122:description:229-262","7122:description:265-336","7122:description:339-415","7122:objective:1-118"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7122:completion:1-11","7122:completion:13-26","7122:completion:31-143"},["opening"]="Minerals were only one reason the Stormpikes wanted the mines. Both armies had hidden excess supplies underground, and killing a mine's opposing leader could secure the stores long enough for guards to arrive.",["pending"]="{actor} would capture a mine outside Stormpike control and report back.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported a captured mine to Durgen.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="4ad8fcb239ff4f8bead1a2f18d799f70d3453f86fa2c434134a2b8c02bddd64f",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7123]={["aftermath"]="The quartermaster welcomed the recruit and raised the prospect of further tasks.",["atomIDs"]={"7123:description:1-110","7123:description:113-150","7123:description:155-250","7123:objective:1-39"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7123:completion:1-9","7123:completion:11-83","7123:completion:85-138"},["opening"]="Jotek sent recruits toward the bunker and its western exit, where the Frostwolf quartermaster waited. His work would lead into the disputed mines beneath the valley.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to speak with the Frostwolf quartermaster.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} answered Jotek's direction and met the quartermaster.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="5bad57a47431a9d37ad62bfcc0db708e31213d02188b552cbd9f3e11d4dea7b0",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7124]={["aftermath"]="Teeka expected friendly guards to make the captured stores and minerals easier to recover.",["atomIDs"]={"7124:description:1-115","7124:description:118-229","7124:description:234-257","7124:description:260-298","7124:description:301-372","7124:description:375-451","7124:objective:1-82"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7124:completion:1-20","7124:completion:22-166","7124:completion:171-185","7124:completion:187-247"},["opening"]="Teeka described Coldtooth and Irondeep as battlefields beneath the battlefield. Their minerals and cached supplies made either worth holding, and taking down the occupying leader would let the Horde station warriors inside.",["pending"]="{actor} would capture a mine for the Horde and return to Teeka.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} reported the mine's capture to Teeka.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="9e7f5129422dd02cd19a25826eeedb7d9f742600f96fb2a2cbcb06e8e5af59d7",["sourceRaceMask"]="178",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7141]={["aftermath"]="Stonehewer believed the general's defeat would give the expedition room to explore.",["atomIDs"]={"7141:description:1-114","7141:description:117-172","7141:description:175-214","7141:description:217-261","7141:description:266-328","7141:description:331-366","7141:objective:1-124"},["bridge"]="The Explorers' League wanted room to investigate Alterac's artifacts. Stonehewer regarded the Frostwolves as the obstacle and sent the campaign south toward Drek'Thar in Frostwolf Keep.",["bridgeFrom"]=7221,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7141:completion:1-14","7141:completion:17-130"},["opening"]="The Explorers' League wanted room to investigate Alterac's artifacts. Stonehewer regarded the Frostwolves as the obstacle and sent the campaign south toward Drek'Thar in Frostwolf Keep.",["pending"]="{actor} would oppose Drek'Thar and report the result to Stonehewer.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed Stonehewer's assignment against Drek'Thar.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="73fe6a038b66a08630e7e4fd7d6358deb9ae47e10fa77e58b24d66848320d9df",["sourceRaceMask"]="77",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7142]={["aftermath"]="Voggah celebrated the opposing general's defeat as a blow to the expedition.",["atomIDs"]={"7142:description:1-95","7142:description:98-176","7142:description:181-248","7142:description:253-291","7142:objective:1-71","7142:objective:74-131"},["bridge"]="Voggah called the Stormpike presence an invasion of Frostwolf territory. His proposed answer reached north to Dun Baldar, where Vanndar Stormpike commanded the opposing force.",["bridgeFrom"]=7222,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7142:completion:1-14","7142:completion:17-65","7142:completion:70-73","7142:completion:76-128"},["opening"]="Voggah called the Stormpike presence an invasion of Frostwolf territory. His proposed answer reached north to Dun Baldar, where Vanndar Stormpike commanded the opposing force.",["pending"]="{actor} meant to confront Vanndar and report to Voggah.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the charge against Vanndar Stormpike.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="b472df5f37997a811ea1b22cbb20aadc433cb3d4f0da2b0d52df7e4e7bfd55f8",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7161]={["aftermath"]="Laggrond acknowledged the initiation and offered the first Frostwolf insignia.",["atomIDs"]={"7161:description:1-9","7161:description:11-92","7161:description:94-166","7161:description:168-193","7161:description:198-264","7161:description:269-332","7161:description:334-370","7161:description:372-443","7161:objective:1-112","7161:objective:114-163"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7161:completion:1-60","7161:completion:62-103","7161:completion:108-144","7161:completion:146-161","7161:completion:166-207","7161:completion:209-317","7161:completion:322-382","7161:completion:384-449"},["opening"]="Laggrond required newcomers to recover a Frostwolf banner from the Wildpaw cavern. The rite offered entry into the clan's wartime ranks, with greater insignias promised for later standing rather than granted at the outset.",["pending"]="{actor} would recover the Frostwolf banner and return to Laggrond.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} brought Laggrond the banner from the Wildpaw cavern.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="bcb92dc382b4bdd39b7337a317e36823e21a7603a94594b542a3a38ec964b719",["sourceRaceMask"]="690",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7162]={["aftermath"]="Haggerdin explained that later standing could earn stronger insignias, with the Eye of Command a distant distinction.",["atomIDs"]={"7162:description:1-32","7162:description:34-76","7162:description:78-122","7162:description:124-156","7162:description:161-253","7162:description:258-316","7162:description:318-371","7162:description:373-410","7162:description:412-485","7162:objective:1-113","7162:objective:115-191"},["endingAtomIDs"]={"7162:completion:1-43","7162:completion:45-109","7162:completion:111-227","7162:completion:232-300","7162:completion:302-367"},["opening"]="Haggerdin's initiation led southwest of Dun Baldar into the Icewing Caverns. Retrieving the planted Stormpike banner would earn the newcomer's insignia before service on the wider field.",["pending"]="{actor} would recover the Stormpike banner for Haggerdin.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} returned the banner to Lieutenant Haggerdin.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="7ba86a0a5237751cb91b56ee6abd5c60c8b85c24c36de98979b652db96335470",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7163]={["aftermath"]="Laggrond urged the bearer to keep the new insignia close and continue serving with honor.",["atomIDs"]={"7163:description:1-33","7163:description:38-57","7163:description:59-188","7163:description:193-202","7163:description:204-236"},["bridge"]="Laggrond's salute marked a change from initiation to recognized friendship with the Frostwolves. Presenting the first insignia would let him acknowledge that standing formally.",["bridgeFrom"]=7161,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7163:completion:1-59","7163:completion:61-88","7163:completion:93-101","7163:completion:103-117"},["opening"]="Laggrond's salute marked a change from initiation to recognized friendship with the Frostwolves. Presenting the first insignia would let him acknowledge that standing formally.",["pending"]="{actor} would present the initiate's insignia to Laggrond.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} exchanged the first insignia with Warmaster Laggrond.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="12dfd3e286e47ff3f8a16edf519bf1cbad998cb014fa5da5b61c16fd1e428c3a",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7164]={["aftermath"]="Laggrond's charge remained the defense of the clan in Drek'Thar's and the Warchief's cause.",["atomIDs"]={"7164:description:1-32","7164:description:34-66","7164:description:68-145","7164:description:150-178","7164:description:180-267","7164:description:272-293"},["bridge"]="Laggrond had not expected every returning soldier to survive. This return merited another rank among the Frostwolves and an insignia to show it.",["bridgeFrom"]=7163,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7164:completion:1-29","7164:completion:42-80","7164:completion:82-102","7164:completion:104-117","7164:completion:119-135"},["opening"]="Laggrond had not expected every returning soldier to survive. This return merited another rank among the Frostwolves and an insignia to show it.",["pending"]="{actor} planned to present the insignia for the next recognition.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the insignia to Laggrond for advancement.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="aabbafae4172fb9dda08ef091f56765eb0d48f7320ecff0bd2fc9d3b495973cd",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7165]={["aftermath"]="Laggrond answered with stories of the soldier's reputation, rather than a new report of a particular battle.",["atomIDs"]={"7165:description:1-16","7165:description:18-84","7165:description:86-120","7165:description:122-162","7165:description:167-208","7165:description:213-234"},["bridge"]="Laggrond described the next distinction as reverence among the guard. His boasts about enemies' fear belonged to his praise; the practical act was the presentation of an insignia for advancement.",["bridgeFrom"]=7164,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7165:completion:1-27","7165:completion:32-92","7165:completion:94-148","7165:completion:150-158"},["opening"]="Laggrond described the next distinction as reverence among the guard. His boasts about enemies' fear belonged to his praise; the practical act was the presentation of an insignia for advancement.",["pending"]="{actor} would take the insignia to Laggrond for recognition.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} completed the insignia exchange with Laggrond.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="02188de748c1cc23a191f85b1ffbc0704d941b60dc7c5460986dd61d2b3edccd",["sourceRaceMask"]="690",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
[7166]={["aftermath"]="Laggrond looked toward command of the field as the next responsibility.",["atomIDs"]={"7166:description:1-39","7166:description:41-120","7166:description:125-148","7166:description:150-169","7166:description:174-195"},["bridge"]="The highest Frostwolf praise now framed Laggrond's summons. Exalted standing was to be reflected in the insignia, while his promise of wider command still lay ahead.",["bridgeFrom"]=7165,["bridgeReplacesSetup"]=true,["endingAtomIDs"]={"7166:completion:1-65","7166:completion:67-117"},["opening"]="The highest Frostwolf praise now framed Laggrond's summons. Exalted standing was to be reflected in the insignia, while his promise of wider command still lay ahead.",["pending"]="{actor} intended to present the insignia to Warmaster Laggrond.",["referenceStatus"]="UNVERIFIED_CLIENT_REFERENCE",["result"]="{actor} presented the insignia for Laggrond's recognition.",["reviewStatus"]="AUTHOR_REVIEWED_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_PENDING",["sourceHash"]="b5fd24deb6bd04927a20ee2544ba0919e3bef61fcafbaf2375cbe7ceb24ef4e0",["sourceRaceMask"]="?",["sourceURL"]="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/questdb/files/9014639"},
